      "name": "TEMPLATE.md",
      "kind": "source",
      "source": "# World Static Map\n\nA joystick-controlled static viewport with editable native .w64 assets and exact per-cell Color RAM rendering.\n\n## Architecture Notes: Why this architecture?\n\nC owns startup, disables the KERNAL cursor IRQ, installs native assets, and calls the independently linked World static renderer.\n\nThe project uses Build Targets so artifact policy stays out of source code. Native assets remain editable and generated C/assembly bindings describe the same bytes. Optional runtime modules are target scoped and dead-strip when they are not selected.\n\n### Change these decisions when\n\n- profiling identifies a measured hot path or memory collision;\n- the target hardware, video standard, or artifact type changes;\n- a project-specific renderer has outgrown the generic extension hook.\n\n### Keep these decisions when\n\n- the change only hides C64 hardware behavior behind another abstraction;\n- it would duplicate bytes already owned by a native Web64 asset;\n- it would move frame-critical work from a bounded assembly path into an unmeasured loop.\n\n## First Modification\n\nOpen assets/maps/world.w64map, edit visible cells and colors, then use fire to exercise visible mutation.\n\n## Project Contract\n\n- Entry: main.c\n- Language: C\n- Compiler ABI: web64-stack-v1\n- Video: PAL\n- Native assets: .w64chr, .w64blk, .w64map, .w64spr\n- Compatibility modules: none\n- Character mode: mono\n- Color RAM: per-cell\n\n\n## References\n\n- semantic-inspiration: [Commodore 64 Programmer Reference Guide](https://archive.org/details/c64-programmer-ref)\n\nThis file belongs to the generated project. Updating the bundled template never mutates this project.\n"
    }
  ]
